<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech CNB sets 26-week bill auction for Wednesday.</title>
<headline>Czech CNB sets 26-week bill auction for Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech National Bank (CNB) said on Tuesday it set a Dutch-style auction of five billion crowns worth of 26-week liqudity bills for Wednesday.</p>
<p>The CNB said the maximum gross yield was set at 12.20 percent, and the maximum net yield would be 9.15 percent.</p>
<p>The six-month Prague interbank offered rate (PRIBOR) stood at 11.89 percent on Tuesday, up one basis point from Monday.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
